# Expectation record for 02_constant_expressions/005_integer_constant_suffixes.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 005_integer_constant_suffixes
area               = 02_constant_expressions
description        = Suffix-driven and base-driven type selection for integer and floating constants at the boundary where a literal no longer fits the default type, observed through _Generic and through folded and volatile-runtime arithmetic including defined unsigned wraparound
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined behaviour and depends on no unspecified behaviour, which is the
precondition both differential oracles rest on rather than a stylistic preference: undefined
behaviour would license either compiler to do anything at all, so a divergence between them would
prove nothing about either. The paragraphs below are the written argument required of every program
in this suite; the warning gate and the sanitizer gate are its machine half.
EVERY LITERAL IS REPRESENTABLE IN THE TYPE C11 6.4.4.1p5 SELECTS FOR IT, so no constant is out of
range for its own type and no constant expression overflows. The decimal literals without a suffix
are within int or within the first type of the signed list that holds them; the hexadecimal and octal
literals without a suffix are within the corresponding list including the unsigned types; and every
suffixed literal is within the type its suffix names.
THE ONLY WRAPPING ARITHMETIC IN THIS PROGRAM IS UNSIGNED, WHICH IS DEFINED RATHER THAN OVERFLOWING.
C11 6.2.5p9 states that a computation involving unsigned operands can never overflow, because a
result that cannot be represented is reduced modulo one greater than the largest representable value.
So 0u - 1u, 0xFFFFFFFFu + 1u, u_zero - 1u and u_max + 1u are fully defined unsigned int operations,
and 0ULL - 1ULL and ull_zero - 1ULL are fully defined unsigned long long operations; the wraparound
they exhibit is the behaviour under test rather than a defect in the test, and all of them are
asserted statically as well as printed.
NO SIGNED EXPRESSION EVER LEAVES ITS RANGE. The widest signed intermediate anywhere is 4294967296,
and it is formed only in a type wider than 32 bits: the unsuffixed decimal constant 4294967295 has a
signed type wide enough to hold it -- long on the LP64 targets, long long on i686, and long long in
the runtime object -- so 4294967295 + 1 is exact rather than wrapping and the line correctly prints 0
for "did it wrap". Nothing approaches INT_MAX in int arithmetic, the one signed product
100000LL * 100000LL is 10000000000 on both the folded and the runtime path, far inside the 64-bit
range C11 guarantees for long long, and no signed value is negated at its minimum.
BOTH SHIFT COUNTS ARE IN RANGE, AND EVERY SHIFT IS A RIGHT SHIFT OF AN UNSIGNED VALUE. The counts are
16 and 32. 0xFFFFFFFFuL >> 16 shifts an unsigned long, which is 32 bits on i686 and 64 bits on the
other three targets, and 16 is strictly below either width; 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFULL >> 32 shifts an
unsigned long long, which is 64 bits everywhere. The runtime twins shift volatile objects of exactly
those types by the same constant counts. Both left operands are unsigned, so no left shift and no
shift of a signed value appears anywhere, and neither the undefined signed-left-shift case nor the
implementation-defined negative-right-shift case can arise. The one division, (0u - 1u) / 3u, has the
non-zero constant divisor 3u and unsigned operands, so it can be neither a division by zero nor the
one signed division C11 leaves undefined, and no remainder operator appears at all.
EVERY CONVERSION THAT COULD NARROW IS WRITTEN WITH AN EXPLICIT CAST, so the conversion is stated in
the source rather than inferred; each such conversion is either value-preserving or a defined modular
reduction of an unsigned value.
_Generic DOES NOT EVALUATE ITS CONTROLLING EXPRESSION (C11 6.5.1.1p2): it selects on the type alone.
Every _Generic here therefore performs no arithmetic at all, which is precisely why the same
constants can be classified and then, separately, used in arithmetic on the fold and runtime lines,
and each association is a small int constant, so no probe can itself misbehave. Every selection has a
matching association or an explicit default, so no _Generic is ill-formed.
EVERY _Static_assert IN THE FILE IS SATISFIED AND TARGET-INVARIANT. Fourteen of them pin the
classifications and the wraparound identities before the program runs, so a mis-typed constant is a
translation failure rather than a silently wrong line. That second half of the claim is a soundness
requirement, not a nicety: an assertion that failed on one target would break that target's build and
destroy the four-way comparison rather than reporting a divergence, and both mandated oracles compare
the observable behaviour of a binary that built successfully. The two-argument form is used
throughout because the message-less spelling is C23 and the default gate's -pedantic -Werror rejects
it.
THERE ARE NO POINTERS AND NO AGGREGATES IN THIS PROGRAM, so no aliasing rule can be broken, no
one-past-the-end pointer can be formed, no subscript is written, no object representation is
inspected, no padding byte can be observed and nothing depends on the addresses of unrelated objects.
Every object is initialized in its own declaration and none is modified afterwards, so no storage is
read uninitialized and nothing is modified twice between two sequence points. Each printf argument is
a _Generic selection, a comparison, or a product of volatile reads; none has a side effect beyond
those reads, each volatile object is read once per expression so the volatile access sequence is
fixed, and no argument's value depends on the order in which the others are evaluated, so the
unspecified order of argument evaluation is unobservable.
LIMITS ARE SPELLED AS LITERALS rather than taken from a header, and limits.h is deliberately not
named: the literals the program needs -- 2147483647, 2147483648, 4294967295, 4294967296,
18446744073709551615 and the hexadecimal and octal forms of the same magnitudes -- are exactly the
boundary values the typing rule turns on, so writing them out is what the program is about, and it
keeps the program single-file reproducible.
NO HEADER IS NAMED ANYWHERE and the single libc prototype the program needs, printf, is declared by
hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`. bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a
bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard I/O header (docs/project-guide.md line 212), so a directive
naming that header would fail on the bcc side of oracle (a) while succeeding on the reference side --
a spurious divergence caused by the test rather than by the compiler under test. Nothing in the file
is a GCC extension, so no include exception and no gate deviation is available to area 02 and none is
needed; the corpus has exactly two header exceptions, area 07's stdarg.h and the dedicated
bundled-header probe in area 12.
THIS RECORD DECLARES NO WARNING-GATE DEVIATION: no ub_audit_flags key appears above, so the program
is audited under the suite's full default gate. It is clean under -Wall -Wextra -pedantic
-Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror at -O0, -O1 and -O2 with all four reference drivers,
and it builds and runs clean under the sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address
-fno-sanitize-recover=all run natively to completion. Both gates are reference-compiler-only and are
never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is untouched.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing. All four targets, all three optimization levels and all three
oracles are enabled, and no expected-divergence marker is attached. These notes exist to
record how that was achieved, because a program in this area could easily have had to narrow:
constant evaluation reaches straight into the type system, which is where the four supported
targets differ.
THE CENTRAL NORMALIZATION, AND THE REASON THIS PROGRAM CAN KEEP ALL FOUR TARGETS. C11 6.4.4.1p5
gives an integer constant the FIRST type in a list that can represent its value, and the list
depends on the spelling: an unsuffixed decimal constant walks int, long, long long, every
candidate SIGNED, while an unsuffixed hexadecimal or octal constant walks int, unsigned int,
long, unsigned long, long long, unsigned long long and so becomes UNSIGNED at a magnitude where
a decimal constant of exactly the same value never does. long is 4 bytes on i686 and 8 bytes on
x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64 (docs/technical-specifications.md target table, lines 457-462), so
the unsuffixed decimal constant 4294967295 legitimately has type long on the three 64-bit targets
and long long on i686. Printing a width -- or asking _Generic to distinguish those two types --
would diverge on i686 through no fault of the compiler. The program asks instead whether the
constant is UNSIGNED, and whether it is one of the two wider SIGNED types, which yields one answer
on every target while still proving the typing rule was applied. No sizeof is printed anywhere in
the file, and no line depends on the width of long or unsigned long.
EVERY CLASSIFICATION WHOSE ANSWER WOULD DIFFER BETWEEN THE FOUR TARGETS IS PRINTED AS A
DISJUNCTION OVER THE CANDIDATE TYPES rather than as a single type test. 4294967296u is unsigned
long on the LP64 targets and unsigned long long on i686, so its line asks whether it took a wider
UNSIGNED type; 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF is likewise tested against unsigned long or unsigned long long
together. The l/L and ul/UL/lu suffix lines name long and unsigned long, which are the types those
suffixes select on every target regardless of how wide they are, so they too are
width-independent.
THE UNSUFFIXED-CONSTANT LINES ARE STABLE FOR THE SAME REASON. 2147483647 and 0x7FFFFFFF are int
on all four; 0x80000000 is unsigned int on all four because a hexadecimal constant may take an
unsigned type; 2147483648 is never unsigned int on any of them, which is what makes
dec_2147483648_is_uint=0 a portable observation rather than a coincidence; and 0177 and 010 are
int everywhere.
EVERY CLAIM IS PRINTED AS OBSERVABLE BEHAVIOUR RATHER THAN AS A WIDTH: a _Generic selection that
names a TYPE, or the value an expression actually computes. That is the distinction that keeps
the program comparable across all four backends, and it is stronger than a width would be,
because the value an expression computes is the thing a user would notice.
long double APPEARS ONLY THROUGH ITS SELECTION BY THE l AND L SUFFIXES, in two _Generic
selections, and never as a value. That is deliberate: no long double VALUE and no long double
width is ever printed, so the MEASURED 16, 12, 16 and 16-byte representations across x86-64,
i686, AArch64 and RISC-V 64 -- x87 80-bit against IEEE binary128 -- cannot reach stdout, whereas
the suffix's type-selection behaviour is fully cross-comparable. The type is therefore covered
here rather than dropped for being awkward, and cross-backend value comparison for it is owned by
13_floating_point/004_long_double_target_restricted.c as a RECORDED EXCLUSION -- oracle_b
disabled, with the measured representations as its basis -- and not as a marker, because an
implementation-defined representation difference is not a divergence attributable to bcc.
WIDTH NORMALIZATION IN THE OUTPUT ITSELF. Every printed value is an int printed with %d -- a
_Generic result or a comparison result, cast where needed -- except the two long long products
printed with %lld, and long long is 64 bits on all four targets. No plain long, no size_t, no
ptrdiff_t, no sizeof result, no address, no pointer value and no floating-point value reaches a
format string, so the measured i686 difference in sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) -- 4 there
against 8 on the other three -- cannot be observed even though this program deliberately reasons
about it.
PLAIN-char SIGNEDNESS. Plain char was MEASURED as signed on x86-64 and i686 and unsigned on
AArch64 and RISC-V 64. No plain-char value is printed, no character data appears, and no printed
line depends on that choice.
_Generic IS RESOLVED ENTIRELY AT TRANSLATION TIME AND THEREFORE HAS NO RUNTIME TWIN BY
CONSTRUCTION, which is correct rather than an omission: there is no run-time object whose type
could be re-examined, so a twin would only re-print the same translation-time answer. The
arithmetic consequences of the selected types DO carry runtime twins -- every fold_ line has a
matching runtime_ line computed from volatile operands holding the same literals, and their
equality is the two-variant assertion -- and at -O2 those twins were measured to emit genuine
instructions (imulq and shrq on x86-64, mul and lsr on AArch64, mul and srli on RISC-V 64) where
the folded forms collapse to immediates. So the suffix's effect on typing is checked by _Generic
and its effect on generated code is checked by the twin; without the twin, optimization would
answer with the constant folder's result and a backend defect in the same computation would never
be asked to appear.
WHAT WOULD LEGITIMATELY BREAK THAT, AND HOW IT MUST THEN BE HANDLED. A conforming target on which
int were not 32 bits, or on which long long were wider than 64, would move a constant into a
different type and change one of these lines without being defective. That would be an
implementation-defined divergence rather than a compiler defect, and it must then be recorded as
an expected divergence with this record's target list narrowed and the reason stated in this
field -- never left to surface as a finding against a backend that did nothing wrong, and never
resolved by deleting the boundary constants, which are the whole subject requirement 2 asks this
program to cover.
EXECUTION CHARACTER SET: NOT ENGAGED, VERIFIED RATHER THAN ASSERTED. C11 5.2.1 leaves the
members of the execution character set and their codes implementation-defined, so a program
that printed a character's numeric code, or rendered a literal as bytes, would owe an
accounting here. This one owes none: it contains no character constant at all -- checked
mechanically, by stripping comments and string literals and finding zero -- and derives no
printed VALUE from a character. Its only string literals are printf format strings and, where
it declares any, _Static_assert messages -- the messages consumed by the compiler and never
emitted, the format strings contributing only fixed label text that is byte-identical in all
twelve cells of the matrix and in the golden above. There is therefore no code to pin and
nothing to narrow. That is precisely what distinguishes this program from 004_sizeof_alignof.c
and 007_string_literal_constants.c in the same area, both of which do print character codes and
both of which pin every code they print with a _Static_assert for that reason.
HERMETIC AND DETERMINISTIC. Every input is a literal in the source: nothing is read from the
clock, the environment, the command line, a file or a socket, and nothing is written anywhere.
Output is one line per semantic property claimed, in a fixed order, so a single divergent line
names the construct that produced it. No address or pointer value is printed, there is no
randomness, no locale-dependent formatting and no data-dependent iteration order, and the
program returns 0 -- well inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is
truncated by the operating system.
MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the reference driver for all four targets at
-O0, -O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one produced these 27 lines
byte-identically with exit status 0, which is why cross-backend comparison is sound, oracle (b)
is enabled with no narrowing, and oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
hex_ffffffff_is_uint=1
dec_4294967295_is_uint=0
dec_4294967295_is_wider_signed=1
dec_2147483647_is_int=1 hex_7fffffff_is_int=1
dec_2147483648_is_uint=0 hex_80000000_is_uint=1
u_dec_2147483648_is_uint=1 u_dec_4294967296_is_uint=0 u_dec_4294967296_is_wider_unsigned=1
hex_max64_is_wider_unsigned=1
u_suffix=1 ll_suffix=1 f_suffix=1
suffix_upper_u=1 suffix_lower_l=1 suffix_upper_l=1
suffix_lower_ll=1 suffix_ul=1 suffix_upper_ul=1 suffix_lu=1
suffix_ull=1 suffix_upper_ull=1 suffix_llu=1
float_upper_f=1 double_no_suffix=1 long_double_lower_l=1 long_double_upper_l=1
octal_0177_is_int=1 octal_010_is_int=1 dec_1_is_int=1
fold_uwrap=1 fold_ullwrap=1
fold_hex_max_plus_one_is_zero=1 fold_dec_max_plus_one_is_zero=0
fold_neg_below_hex_boundary=0 fold_neg_below_dec_boundary=1
fold_ll_product=10000000000
fold_ul_shift=1 fold_ull_shift=1
fold_octal_0177_is_127=1 fold_octal_010_is_8=1
fold_udiv=1
runtime_uwrap=1 runtime_ullwrap=1
runtime_hex_max_plus_one_is_zero=1 runtime_dec_max_plus_one_is_zero=0
runtime_neg_below_hex_boundary=0 runtime_neg_below_dec_boundary=1
runtime_ll_product=10000000000
runtime_ul_shift=1 runtime_ull_shift=1
runtime_octal_0177_is_127=1 runtime_octal_010_is_8=1
runtime_udiv=1
END
